    "font" : "SFRM1095",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "fn : H1(Kn,p,E[p∞]) −→ H1(K∞,p,E[p∞])Gal(K∞,p/Fn,p) = H1(K∞,p,E[p∞])[ωn] is injective. Since the map fn± is the restriction of fn to H±1 (Kn,p,E[p∞]), fn± is also injective. For the claim for Coker fn±, it suﬃces to show that both the Zp-coranks of H±1 (Kn,p,E[p∞])"
  }, {
