    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "On the other hand, we have H±1 (Kn,p,E[p∞]) = E(Kn,p)± ⊗ (Qp /Zp) by the deﬁnition. Thus, we see that H±1 (Kn,p,E[p∞])∨ ≃ Λ2n/ωn±Λ2n by Proposition 3.4. Therefore, the Zp-rank of H±1 (Kn,p,E[p∞]) and H±1 (K∞,w,E[p∞])[ωn±] are the same."
